␀␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:   RPC commands will likely fail.  Recovery procedure:
␀␀E (%lu) %s:     1. From this source tree, build the CP firmware:
␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:          cd examples/system/get_cp_fw_version/cp
␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:          idf.py set-target <cp_chip> && idf.py build
␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:        Save build/eh_cp_*.bin outside the repo.
␀␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:     2. Identify the commit your CP firmware was built from
␀E (%lu) %s:        (CP boot log / release notes).  If you cannot identify
␀␀E (%lu) %s:        a mapped commit for your CP firmware, contact your CP
␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:        firmware provider.  git checkout <that_commit>.
␀E (%lu) %s:     3. Build the host driver + app from that older commit, load
␀␀␀␀E (%lu) %s:        it, and OTA the CP with the binary saved in step 1.
␀E (%lu) %s:     4. git checkout <this_branch>; rebuild the host; reconnect.
